ing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commit/ce51c65f094573c30a825fa081364a4dc6efc22a","node_id":"C_kwDOP_6DBNoAKGNlNTFjNjVmMDk0NTczYzMwYTgyNWZhMDgxMzY0YTRkYzZlZmMyMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commit/b7f4d0cf48df6a8340a33d2d6389794d755ff6a1","sha":"b7f4d0cf48df6a8340a33d2d6389794d755ff6a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/b7f4d0cf48df6a8340a33d2d6389794d755ff6a1"}],"sha":"ce51c65f094573c30a825fa081364a4dc6efc22a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/ce51c65f094573c30a825fa081364a4dc6efc22a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56585589?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/d-rom","id":56585589,"login":"d-rom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NTg1NTg5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/b7f4d0cf48df6a8340a33d2d6389794d755ff6a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:46:10Z","email":"daria.marassanova@varda.ag","name":"Daria Ruiz-Ogarrio Marassanova"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:46:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: support categorical values (#876)\n\n- `GET /soil-data` now provides an additional nullable field\n\"value_label\" (for \"Explore\" and export jobs)\n- `GET /datasets/.../soil-data` (Preview step) Replaces the values by\ntheir category labels where applies. The behaviour is different from the\nendpoint described above as this is still raw data that was already\naccepted in any given type (although cleaned afterwards), so the\nfrontend doesn''t break when receiving string values. Even though this\npreview is the output of `VectorDataLoad.getDataPreview`, same as the\nbulk-load job, which then runs `POST /soil-data` on this output, the\ncategory values are substituted in the output afterwards, so both paths\nwork (bulk-load doesn''t receive the category labels as `POST /soil-data`\ndoesn''t accept them).\n- Data cleaning supports mapping labels, aliases and codes as string to\ntheir category code (number). Drops unsupported categories and tracks\nthis in the cleaning summary.\n- `POST soil-data` now supports 0 values for categories where applies,\nif category doesn''t exist or value is not numeric it throws an error and\nskips the whole record.\n- Category mappings are now maintained through a CSV and synced with the\nrest of vocabularies.\n- Exported raster files include the mapping embedded in their metadata,\nas well as an auxiliary sidecar file (for GeoTIFF only) that displays\nthe legend in QGIS:\n<img width=\"405\" height=\"258\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5840cc86-9ae5-45f9-ba1b-c788ed98ff88\"\n/>\n\n- Now, for raster load and ingest, the source of truth for whether a\nlayer is categorical or continuous is whether soil_property.classes\nstores a mapping (in that moment, so if between ingest and export the\nsoil_property classes have been populated and the request has a\ntargetCrs, the file would be reprojected with the nearest neighbour\nalgorithm).\n- (unrelated fix) Raster export as GPKG when targetCrs is set and only\none layer is exported generates a GeoTIFF named as GPKG.\n- (unrelated docs) Document raster export output.\n\n### To do:\n- FE change to display value_label in \"Data explorer\" where applies. -\nTBC\n- Apply in [raster\npreview](https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/pull/875).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: svaccari <stefano.vaccari@varda.ag>","tree":{"sha":"a33c06501bf205da67c1ccf2018c08eda1fb1271","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/trees/a33c06501bf205da67c1ccf2018c08eda1fb1271"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/commits/b7f4d0cf48df6a8340a33d2d6389794d755ff6a1","verification":{"payload":"tree a33c06501bf205da67c1ccf2018c08eda1fb1271\nparent c90e7867db72045ae49da86ca63eaed88e222e31\nauthor Daria Ruiz-Ogarrio Marassanova <daria.marassanova@varda.ag> 1791359170 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791359170 +0200\n\nfeat: support categorical values (#876)\n\n- `GET /soil-data` now provides an additional nullable field\n\"value_label\" (for \"Explore\" and export jobs)\n- `GET /datasets/.../soil-data` (Preview step) Replaces the values by\ntheir category labels where applies. The behaviour is different from the\nendpoint described above as this is still raw data that was already\naccepted in any given type (although cleaned afterwards), so the\nfrontend doesn''t break when receiving string values. Even though this\npreview is the output of `VectorDataLoad.getDataPreview`, same as the\nbulk-load job, which then runs `POST /soil-data` on this output, the\ncategory values are substituted in the output afterwards, so both paths\nwork (bulk-load doesn''t receive the category labels as `POST /soil-data`\ndoesn''t accept them).\n- Data cleaning supports mapping labels, aliases and codes as string to\ntheir category code (number). Drops unsupported categories and tracks\nthis in the cleaning summary.\n- `POST soil-data` now supports 0 values for categories where applies,\nif category doesn''t exist or value is not numeric it throws an error and\nskips the whole record.\n- Category mappings are now maintained through a CSV and synced with the\nrest of vocabularies.\n- Exported raster files include the mapping embedded in their metadata,\nas well as an auxiliary sidecar file (for GeoTIFF only) that displays\nthe legend in QGIS:\n<img width=\"405\" height=\"258\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5840cc86-9ae5-45f9-ba1b-c788ed98ff88\"\n/>\n\n- Now, for raster load and ingest, the source of truth for whether a\nlayer is categorical or continuous is whether soil_property.classes\nstores a mapping (in that moment, so if between ingest and export the\nsoil_property classes have been populated and the request has a\ntargetCrs, the file would be reprojected with the nearest neighbour\nalgorithm).\n- (unrelated fix) Raster export as GPKG when targetCrs is set and only\none layer is exported generates a GeoTIFF named as GPKG.\n- (unrelated docs) Document raster export output.\n\n### To do:\n- FE change to display value_label in \"Data explorer\" where applies. -\nTBC\n- Apply in [raster\npreview](https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/pull/875).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: svaccari <stefano.vaccari@varda.ag>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxfjDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiFUQAHMR7Hp+8Nij0eCKOMOia/Zd\nnRT75RjpVWe63Ruy64qDWrx7JYTmbE8SP5Ih2zwigtv