-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commit/4d5d058c67404a4a9ecc70b80cc83139b850c670","node_id":"C_kwDOP_6DBNoAKDRkNWQwNThjNjc0MDRhNGE5ZWNjNzBiODBjYzgzMTM5Yjg1MGM2NzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commit/dfa3225c24adc50a582279401a6dc5e6ea7272f7","sha":"dfa3225c24adc50a582279401a6dc5e6ea7272f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/dfa3225c24adc50a582279401a6dc5e6ea7272f7"}],"sha":"4d5d058c67404a4a9ecc70b80cc83139b850c670","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/4d5d058c67404a4a9ecc70b80cc83139b850c670"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/153092107?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cristbello","id":153092107,"login":"cristbello","node_id":"U_kgDOCSAACw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/dfa3225c24adc50a582279401a6dc5e6ea7272f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:17:06Z","email":"153092107+cristbello@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cristbello"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:17:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: sp-5524 share useFilter with plugins, drop mapSelection from PluginContext (#856)\n\n## Summary\n\nPlugins can now fetch a stored filter by id through\n`PluginContext.useFilter`. This replaces `PluginContext.mapSelection`,\nwhich is removed. Every host-backed query hook in the context now\nreports the real `isError` instead of a hard-coded `false`.\n\nSee https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-plugins/pull/30 to test this\nmanually.\n\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"1056\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-28 at 16 11 36\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19169d92-7538-426b-89d5-9567ec4c3156\"\n/>\n\n## Changes\n\n### New `useFilter` hook\n- `frontend/src/hooks/useFilter.ts`: new hook. It calls `GET\n/data-filters/:id`, stays disabled until `filterId` is set, and uses\n`retry: false` because a missing filter is a 404 that retrying won''t\nfix.\n- Plugins get it as `context.useFilter(filterId)`, which returns\n`PluginQueryResult<PluginStoredDataFilter>`.\n- The plugin wrapper passes through only `id`, `name`,\n`filter.geometries` and `filter.parameters`. The filter''s owner doesn''t\nreach plugins.\n- New `PluginStoredDataFilter` type in\n`frontend-plugin-types/filter.ts`.\n\n### `mapSelection` removed from `PluginContext` ⚠️ breaking for plugins\n- Removed `mapSelection`, `PluginMapSelection`, `PluginLngLat` and\n`PluginGeoJSONFeature` from `frontend-plugin-types`.\n- `usePluginContext` no longer reads `useAvailabilityMap`, so its memo\nnow depends only on `user`. The context identity no longer changes on\nevery map selection change.\n- To get the host''s selection now, a plugin is linked with a\n`?filterId=` query parameter and reads it back with\n`context.useFilter(filterId)`. A `--with-map` plugin uses its own\n`selectionState`.\n\n### Real `isError` through `PluginContext`\n- `useDataFilterQuery`, `useFilteredCoverageQuery` and `useRaster` now\nreturn `isError`.\n- `ThemeContext` now exposes `isThemeConfigError` and `isLogoError`. A\nmissing logo (404) still resolves to `null` and is not treated as an\nerror.\n- In `usePluginContext`, `useTheme`, `useDataFilterQuery`,\n`useFilteredCoverageQuery` and `useRasterCategories` pass these through\ninstead of returning `isError: false`.\n\n### Plugin example and docs\n- `frontend-plugin-example`: removed `mapSelection` usage. `mockContext`\nnow provides a mock `useFilter` with a sample stored filter.\n- `docs/frontend/plugin-development.md`: new \"Fetching a stored filter\"\nsection. The selection info card row now points to `selectionState` or\n`useFilter`.\n- `docs/frontend/hooks-reference.md`: added `useFilter`.\n- ADR 0027: replaced the `mapSelection` references.\n- `Routes.tsx`: updated the comment about what changes `PluginContext`''s\nidentity (now only `user`).\n\n## Tests\n- New `frontend/tests/hooks/useFilter.test.ts`.\n- `usePluginContext.test.ts` updated for `useFilter`, the removed\n`mapSelection`, and `isError` passthrough.\n- `isError` coverage added to the `useDataFilterQuery`,\n`useFilteredCoverageQuery`, `useRaster` and `useTheme` tests.\n\n## Migration note for plugin authors\nIf your plugin reads `context.mapSelection`, it will stop compiling\nafter you re-sync `frontend-plugin-types`. Link to the plugin with a\n`filterId` and use `context.useFilter(filterId)` instead.","tree":{"sha":"b50fbed388ae1c98a5ef2bc3405e2e0d93675562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/trees/b50fbed388ae1c98a5ef2bc3405e2e0d93675562"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/commits/dfa3225c24adc50a582279401a6dc5e6ea7272f7","verification":{"payload":"tree b50fbed388ae1c98a5ef2bc3405e2e0d93675562\nparent 56f4b95ce1b1f62ce5b7e602c6e28e389b218cc3\nauthor cristbello <153092107+cristbello@users.noreply.github.com> 1790666226 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790666226 +0200\n\nfeat: sp-5524 share useFilter with plugins, drop mapSelection from PluginContext (#856)\n\n## Summary\n\nPlugins can now fetch a stored filter by id through\n`PluginContext.useFilter`. This replaces `PluginContext.mapSelection`,\nwhich is removed. Every host-backed query hook in the context now\nreports the real `isError` instead of a hard-coded `false`.\n\nSee https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-plugins/pull/30 to test this\nmanually.\n\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"1056\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-28 at 16 11 36\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19169d92-7538-426b-89d5-9567ec4c3156\"\n/>\n\n## Changes\n\n### New `useFilter` hook\n- `frontend/src/hooks/useFilter.ts`: new hook. It calls `GET\n/data-filters/:id`, stays disabled until `filterId` is set, and uses\n`retry: false` because a missing filter is a 404 that retrying won''t\nfix.\n- Plugins get it as `context.useFilter(filterId)`, which returns\n`PluginQueryResult<PluginStoredDataFilter>`.\n- The plugin wrapper passes through only `id`, `name`,\n`filter.geometries` and `filter.parameters`. The filter''s owner doesn''t\nreach plugins.\n- New `PluginStoredDataFilter` type in\n`frontend-plugin-types/filter.ts`.\n\n### `mapSelection` removed from `PluginContext` ⚠️ breaking for plugins\n- Removed `mapSelection`, `PluginMapSelection`, `PluginLngLat` and\n`PluginGeoJSONFeature` from `frontend-plugin-types`.\n- `usePluginContext` no longer reads `useAvailabilityMap`, so its memo\nnow depends only on `user`. The context identity no longer changes on\nevery map selection change.\n- To get the host''s selection now, a plugin is linked with a\n`?filterId=` query parameter and reads it back with\n`context.useFilter(filterId)`. A `--with-map` plugin uses its own\n`selectionState`.\n\n### Real `isError` through `PluginContext`\n- `useDataFilterQuery`, `useFilteredCoverageQuery` and `useRaster` now\nreturn `isError`.\n- `ThemeContext` now exposes `isThemeConfigError` and `isLogoError`. A\nmissing logo (404) still resolves to `null` and is not treated as an\nerror.\n- In `usePluginContext`, `useTheme`, `useDataFilterQuery`,\n`useFilteredCoverageQuery` and `useRasterCategories` pass these through\ninstead of returning `isError: false`.\n\n### Plugin example and docs\n- `frontend-plugin-example`: removed `mapSelection` usage. `mockContext`\nnow provides a mock `useFilter` with a sample stored filter.\n- `docs/frontend/plugin-development.md`: new \"Fetching a stored filter\"\nsection. The selection info card row now points to `selectionState` or\n`useFilter`.\n- `docs/frontend/hooks-reference.md`: added `useFilter`.\n- ADR 0027: replaced the `mapSelection` references.\n- `Routes.tsx`: updated the comment about what changes `PluginContext`''s\nidentity (now only `user`).\n\n## Tests\n- New `frontend/tests/hooks/useFilter.test.ts`.\n- `usePluginContext.test.ts` updated for `useFilter`, the removed\n`mapSelection`, and `isError` passthrough.\n- `isError` coverage added to the `useDataFilterQuery`,\n`useFilteredCoverageQuery`, `useRaster` and `useTheme` tests.\n\n## Migration note for plugin authors\nIf your plugin reads `context.mapSelection`, it will stop compiling\nafter you re-sync `frontend-plugin-types`. Link to the plugin with a\n`filterId` and use `context.useFilter(filterId)` instead.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu2XyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5Y4QADSXWdTc5POA3v6VaZBZn20V\n8cPZ4qRWUt0Jp2y6gAAhuB/Q/+tRa4prBW0aUpdX2QH3Dwc/udKUQ0ygqSMAhPPr\nbUXwISoOTgLjNT+6IYp1VQPGU3nhw2Ft2YREUkpRRwFVYwz6oQXJsiNASw6/iVns\n8r8rAfQWQ1WIK9eaChPg+Z0p9lrqW8JuLoBIgKrmo3fYzfJfmdmcd+FvM1ibNw0k\nD0RpOAWD5TPDFCq6AWNHftcQtqWJQvrl9zUp4tr4+V1X+k9v0CQ3hnRaYFtLIk+