":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cristbello","id":153092107,"login":"cristbello","node_id":"U_kgDOCSAACw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cristbello","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/9a6166040cf0098b038df89c21be3d556b6fcc32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T07:02:12Z","email":"153092107+cristbello@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cristbello"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T07:02:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: sp-5678 delegate nested plugin routes to plugin router, stop recreating it, and share react-router with plugins (#841)\n\nPlugin routes were registered as an exact path match (\"/dashboards\"), so\nany deeper URL (e.g. \"/dashboards/list\") never matched and fell through\nto the app-wide catch-all, redirecting to \"/\". Register with a trailing\n\"/*\" so the plugin''s own router handles its sub-paths.\n\nStop rebuilding the host''s createBrowserRouter instance whenever\nusePluginContext()''s return value changes identity (e.g. on map\nselection state), since RouterProvider only resyncs on a router identity\nchange and a swap mid-flight can leave a route element rendered against\na stale router.\n\nAlso register react-router as a shared Module Federation singleton\n(mf.registerShared, alongside react/react-dom/i18next/react-i18next).\nPlugins like dashboards already declare it as a shared singleton\ndependency, but the host never provided it, so each plugin fell back to\nits own separate react-router module instance — with its own separate\nNavigationContext. Once the dashboards plugin stopped wrapping itself in\nits own <BrowserRouter> (previous commit), its nested <Routes> had no\nway to see the host''s Router context at all, throwing \"useRoutes() may\nbe used only in the context of a <Router> component.\"","tree":{"sha":"14475b0876a153b6aca1d409d5edfbb2af6f6180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/trees/14475b0876a153b6aca1d409d5edfbb2af6f6180"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/commits/9a6166040cf0098b038df89c21be3d556b6fcc32","verification":{"payload":"tree 14475b0876a153b6aca1d409d5edfbb2af6f6180\nparent 5e3674ac75f542e5da46ef6b92f750e3813e1f8f\nauthor cristbello <153092107+cristbello@users.noreply.github.com> 1790146932 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790146932 +0200\n\nfix: sp-5678 delegate nested plugin routes to plugin router, stop recreating it, and share react-router with plugins (#841)\n\nPlugin routes were registered as an exact path match (\"/dashboards\"), so\nany deeper URL (e.g. \"/dashboards/list\") never matched and fell through\nto the app-wide catch-all, redirecting to \"/\". Register with a trailing\n\"/*\" so the plugin''s own router handles its sub-paths.\n\nStop rebuilding the host''s createBrowserRouter instance whenever\nusePluginContext()''s return value changes identity (e.g. on map\nselection state), since RouterProvider only resyncs on a router identity\nchange and a swap mid-flight can leave a route element rendered against\na stale router.\n\nAlso register react-router as a shared Module Federation singleton\n(mf.registerShared, alongside react/react-dom/i18next/react-i18next).\nPlugins like dashboards already declare it as a shared singleton\ndependency, but the host never provided it, so each plugin fell back to\nits own separate react-router module instance — with its own separate\nNavigationContext. Once the dashboards plugin stopped wrapping itself in\nits own <BrowserRouter> (previous commit), its nested <Routes> had no\nway to see the host''s Router context at all, throwing \"useRoutes() may\nbe used only in the context of a <Router> component.\"","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs3l0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATxAQAA6I5qRFZb4nl249M0n/jdrS\nnCEpq2mjuYLvahHJlqr10D49Hq2AeSdTpOjHOSvhALGCyltgxrXkiirD2uWIw0qk\n9c9Ozn8iaJCVVHJUQuzdbvGguEfhzQUECQfpT/WwWOv3n4lN6r00+kTjyAQ+r2Kc\ntOdVqZWa+kzxMPfWr4xl9jE7Ck2JrfTn5P5/2KSzMy9qUKh+nBeEHQUV6OcCiW1W\nv1iwgVXEgsdXXWzdI7V8d2wV5yS3/XjTy7Voe0JfqPZLJDZUDtlA4IGGJdvqqlD5\nQLxOj10LctoYLXQ8jH7hkTsY6vZV2gtOMCVxY44FKjuekv30fyJowraqKSekxGEJ\nwhqiH1uByZ2n4TlkxtFppRvj1ba7912q3CpNk6AplfJZ5Wr6ks91LK27b0xCXVJe\nTNXZ9XZxSs8j/dfbRT4wv2IAaJOp16vfdCgJA8frF+XHZvfphzxWWIxFpPBxCfq0\ntvlBgHaeOtdy7+nx94+TQ31oozpgwRoMp/Qcu9WyoVJMLHmwpoQ+7n5Tk3eEHa6l\nrV7RlFewS5lbZ4dsoKbjQD2gQpHgFR/OiBRG8W+UXtxoRNtu92Mc3DmtOvI8sVOk\nbGYYrbpmn+PZIP7jNd/nsrBdmSTijlq451yfIb4LIa+3U1/pUzv1iHbgj77C4ZyV\npy4O4zwreJoxAjCoShHJ\n=dSOi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T07:02:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","