1db0798a66439983a7c370fa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/b64de3d21e78a141db0798a66439983a7c370fa5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232349910?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/VardAlb","id":232349910,"login":"VardAlb","node_id":"U_kgDODdlg1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/43a3307a2ee57975369025f1c5fafcc7eed3cd98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:05:02Z","email":"alberto.arpini@varda.ag","name":"VardAlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:05:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: sp-5650 add batch config fetching hooks (#829)\n\n## Summary\nAdd a batch path for config fetching that mirrors the existing single-id\n`useConfig`/`usePluginConfig` pair. The backend gained `GET\n/config?ids=...`\n(PR #828); the frontend had no way to call it.\n\n- `useConfigs(ids)` — host-level hook, calls `GET /config` with a\ncomma-separated `ids` parameter, returns `{ data, isLoading, isError }`.\n  Read-only, no `saveConfig`.\n- `usePluginConfigs(pluginId, ids)` — plugin-facing wrapper. Namespaces\nids\nas `plugin:{pluginId}:{id}`, then strips the prefix from the response so\n  plugins see their own unprefixed ids.\n- `PluginContext.usePluginConfigs` added to `frontend-plugin-types`,\nwith a\n  matching static mock in `frontend-plugin-example`.\n- Wired into `usePluginContext`, passed through unchanged.\n- Docs: new \"Batch-fetching multiple config ids\" section in\n  `plugin-development.md`.","tree":{"sha":"dfc2b18431b6669cbfc166beb9c88775ae44466d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/trees/dfc2b18431b6669cbfc166beb9c88775ae44466d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/commits/43a3307a2ee57975369025f1c5fafcc7eed3cd98","verification":{"payload":"tree dfc2b18431b6669cbfc166beb9c88775ae44466d\nparent 0abdd3b3a2cb5f929328d8d3cde4cd01209a2d00\nauthor VardAlb <alberto.arpini@varda.ag> 1789481102 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789481102 +0200\n\nfeat: sp-5650 add batch config fetching hooks (#829)\n\n## Summary\nAdd a batch path for config fetching that mirrors the existing single-id\n`useConfig`/`usePluginConfig` pair. The backend gained `GET\n/config?ids=...`\n(PR #828); the frontend had no way to call it.\n\n- `useConfigs(ids)` — host-level hook, calls `GET /config` with a\ncomma-separated `ids` parameter, returns `{ data, isLoading, isError }`.\n  Read-only, no `saveConfig`.\n- `usePluginConfigs(pluginId, ids)` — plugin-facing wrapper. Namespaces\nids\nas `plugin:{pluginId}:{id}`, then strips the prefix from the response so\n  plugins see their own unprefixed ids.\n- `PluginContext.usePluginConfigs` added to `frontend-plugin-types`,\nwith a\n  matching static mock in `frontend-plugin-example`.\n- Wired into `usePluginContext`, passed through unchanged.\n- Docs: new \"Batch-fetching multiple config ids\" section in\n  `plugin-development.md`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqVCOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsYcQAAb1HxFFBFTTOmXhilK8OLaR\nMNosWd6a1B/N3h/nQY1hr44G/ds97cfaSMcnUXL/b+Zuy9pkMgsEVjhjN13wKA/q\nvyGBa1aaeBU1xRMDlSvMh/yh8EttAruN6FA