dlg1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/a3cbac360d3f09612c116fc6183bca1c0eb07786/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:25:39Z","email":"alberto.arpini@varda.ag","name":"VardAlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T09:25:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: sp-5632 add scope to entitlements (#825)\n\n## Summary\nEntitlements storage and the `GET /entitlements` response change from a\nflat map keyed by dataset slug to a map namespaced by scope:\n`{\"datasets\": {...}, \"configs\": {...}}`. This lets a new `configs` scope\nexist without colliding with dataset slugs. `GET /entitlements` gains a\nmandatory `scope` query parameter (`datasets` | `configs` |\n`dashboards`); the endpoint returns only that scope''s sub-map. Existing\nrows are migrated in place. Backend and frontend ship together as a hard\ncutover.\n\nThe external `ENTITLEMENTS_ENDPOINT` service is not affected: its flat\nresponse is wrapped under `datasets` internally.\n\n## Changes\n- `Capability` enum gains `READ` and `WRITE` (additive only).\n- Migration nests existing `data` under `datasets` and replaces the\nsingle GIN index with two scoped indexes,\n`idx_entitlements_data_datasets_gin` and\n`idx_entitlements_data_configs_gin`.\n- `EntitlementService` methods (`getEntityEntitlements`,\n`setEntityEntitlements`, `deleteEntityEntitlements`,\n`enforceEntitlements`) take an explicit scope parameter and read/write\nthe matching sub-object.\n- `GET /entitlements` requires `scope`; missing or invalid values return\n400.\n- Downstream consumers of `requestData.entitlements` are updated to read\nfrom the `datasets` sub-map.\n- Frontend `useEntitlements` takes an optional `scope` parameter and\nfetches only when one is passed, to avoid an unneeded network call from\ncall sites that only check the static role matrix. See ADR-0033 for the\nreasoning.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"488802cc577cb58a2c1117b252c4007578ad7ed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/trees/488802cc577cb58a2c1117b252c4007578ad7ed7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/commits/a3cbac360d3f09612c116fc6183bca1c0eb07786","verification":{"payload":"tree 488802cc577cb58a2c1117b252c4007578ad7ed7\nparent 7f717636aa726c53d4bc733cbbfc2ebc3d49ec41\nauthor VardAlb <alberto.arpini@varda.ag> 1789377939 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789377939 +0200\n\nfeat: sp-5632 add scope to entitlements (#825)\n\n## Summary\nEntitlements storage and the `GET /entitlements` response change from a\nflat map keyed by dataset slug to a map namespaced by scope:\n`{\"datasets\": {...}, \"configs\": {...}}`. This lets a new `configs` scope\nexist without colliding with dataset slugs. `GET /entitlements` gains a\nmandatory `scope` query parameter (`datasets` | `configs` |\n`dashboards`); the endpoint returns only that scope''s sub-map. Existing\nrows are migrated in place. Backend and frontend ship together as a hard\ncutover.\n\nThe external `ENTITLEMENTS_ENDPOINT` service is not affected: its flat\nresponse is wrapped under `datasets` internally.\n\n## Changes\n- `Capability` enum gains `READ` and `WRITE` (additive only).\n- Migration nests existing `data` under `datasets` and replaces the\nsingle GIN index with two scoped indexes,\n`idx_entitlements_data_datasets_gin` and\n`idx_entitlements_data_configs_gin`.\n- `EntitlementService` methods (`getEntityEntitlements`,\n`setEntityEntitlements`, `deleteEntityEntitlements`,\n`enforceEntitlements`) take an explicit scope parameter and read/write\nthe matching sub-object.\n- `GET /entitlements` requires `scope`; missing or invalid values return\n400.\n- Downstream consumers of `requestData.entitlements` are updated to read\nfrom the `datasets` sub-map.\n- Frontend `useEntitlements` takes an optional `scope` parameter and\nfetches only when one is passed, to avoid an unneeded network call from\ncall sites that only check the static role matrix. See ADR-0033 for the\nreasoning.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp72TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcF4QAGdKHpJh5IueL/ALECkgV0no\nTY8rXZJth2wxxF/kTm9Rt2MxpdfAAzNMYU8UMpBsRJbcyTnUXJ66lcMWm+1nkk+I\nEyGmzVN1JiqCmhZTUIRFG+YSota9QxlWCFniq4yiE884/X/k4ZJhlziq1iPQ86Ph\nVG9CETdnfX/MosxoCs2alck+3cqlyXToTl59aappdayVS9E8i5V340p3svDNp20f\no53deVc7PPC3+/bILOsLHpeG6UVq70ZQqqEpmr13KUUXBgF+dQKXpgbz4n3XI/8f\ncpIVY6shFZfefDxoWLgy8f5nU4dBQ4OVua8Kbmgd5F+XioAnLV9qKmfUgL2DX8+4\nUFdGgsikPjFJGpLVkz3Zk3EZovA5hSYDFJ0G76eA3bP79j27EkCqR7fqD39THdYC\nGP+AIRU6/W6Zy9U2+6h/3N2rAJzC1fIwPVrvDJVbkniX4BOVSLDhU06asGnTexpQ\nhF+IHy4A8DM8bYzDx3mnOO9+dEVdmQhpfD9Xqt8Xq4Ps/HbDPjElPwg9Op4Ixl7m\ndkEFnvMhaQJizj5yAm+4evatWR1ru/qoHo7FwsqHPfvqcRP+rbMwURvOHtquChX2\nAEhgHxU0g/rfYYF92RyaYWcHEkl/dLbLt5cXLPz68Nx5sW4pTNYOvVkvcMLMZrDN\nJPAJF9WSGNQ8zKd/yc6e\n=GZ9j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T09:25:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node