llowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/d-rom","id":56585589,"login":"d-rom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NTg1NTg5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/a48ae38c87ab8a5918cebdad77825b7548ac1ad1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:35:52Z","email":"daria.marassanova@varda.ag","name":"Daria Ruiz-Ogarrio Marassanova"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:35:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: raster load to use gdal_footprint concurrently, insert footprints as WKB (#818)\n\nChanges to raster-load process:\n- Replace fixed `INSERT_FOOTPRINT_BATCH` size with accumulated\n`MAX_BATCH_VERTICES` (and `MAX_BATCH_FOOTPRINTS` as backstop).\n- Encode each footprint as WKB rather than `JSON.stringify`, and inserts\nvia `ST_GeomFromWKB` rather\n  than `ST_GeomFromGeoJSON`.\n- Moved footprint extraction from the same process and event-loop as the\nAPI server to a GDAL subprocess (`gdal_footprint`), which does not\nsupport windowed reads out of the box. -> Input (tile VRT) is created in\nJS (to avoid an additional GDAL subprocess spawning per tile).\n`gdal_footprint` already handles previously addressed issues related to\nNoData rounding precision error and collapsing collinear points.\n- Implemented concurrency in footprint extraction over windows of\n`FOOTPRINT_CONCURRENCY` tiles.\n- The overview extraction step now always runs, including for\nlocal-storage-mode rasters, as the tile VRT needs the file it points to\nto be single-band and single-resolution.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: svaccari <stefano.vaccari@varda.ag>","tree":{"sha":"9ea3ee68c80a9e0874fefddf62ef52e8e243cde7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/trees/9ea3ee68c80a9e0874fefddf62ef52e8e243cde7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/commits/a48ae38c87ab8a5918cebdad77825b7548ac1ad1","verification":{"payload":"tree 9ea3ee68c80a9e0874fefddf62ef52e8e243cde7\nparent 7872555d5028a55073e05175697909277a9aaa3f\nauthor Daria Ruiz-Ogarrio Marassanova <daria.marassanova@varda.ag> 1789112152 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789112152 +0200\n\nfix: raster load to use gdal_footprint concurrently, insert footprints as WKB (#818)\n\nChanges to raster-load process:\n- Replace fixed `INSERT_FOOTPRINT_BATCH` size with accumulated\n`MAX_BATCH_VERTICES` (and `MAX_BATCH_FOOTPRINTS` as backstop).\n- Encode each footprint as WKB rather than `JSON.stringify`, and inserts\nvia `ST_GeomFromWKB` rather\n  than `ST_GeomFromGeoJSON`.\n- Moved footprint extraction from the same process and event-loop as the\nAPI server to a GDAL subprocess (`gdal_footprint`), which does not\nsupport windowed reads out of the box. -> Input (tile VRT) is created in\nJS (to avoid an additional GDAL subprocess spawning per tile).\n`gdal_footprint` already handles previously addressed issues related to\nNoData rounding precision error and collapsing collinear points.\n- Implemented concurrency in footprint extraction over windows of\n`FOOTPRINT_CONCURRENCY` tiles.\n- The overview extraction step now always runs, including for\nlocal-storage-mode rasters, as the tile VRT needs the file it points to\nto be single-band and single-resolution.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: svaccari <stefano.vaccari@varda.ag>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo69YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/Z8QAGsr2N7GTWDylXVk1EhSRYgq\nvAKfcWDcii68w