steps component extension (#814)\n\n- Steps component was extended to render \"horizontal\" and \"vertical\"\nlayouts of steps controlled by \"orientation\" prop.\n- Also \"showCompletedIcon\" - new property (true by default) that used to\nset if we want show or hide check icon on completed steps.\n- css variables --active-icon-color, --active-icon-background-color,\n--active-title-color were added to have easy control on the colors from\noutside the component with className\n\n<img width=\"1310\" height=\"194\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-28 at 10 33 03\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b437a5e9-8ac9-4dbf-a83e-13534ca1e79c\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1107\" height=\"184\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-28 at 10 33 18\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b7c85783-6f0e-4e11-9ffa-70aec1e11720\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1006\" height=\"191\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-28 at 10 33 36\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ec93edd-a2a8-4ef5-b853-d7b8f628705b\"\n/>\n<img width=\"945\" height=\"144\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-28 at 10 34 34\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cd89a1b6-3789-4423-9e44-0e05ba6158b0\"\n/>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkX/1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqvIQAGufXavBwanvGX87g4Vm7Nop\nPgMy0Qqsm41YBD42QPSWcVHg9osbPDOVxPVw8sGl4laQFT0+Bqz3mKvaOpyzICng\nAQOmc2mWJK1gdICPbd59jhrhpZ98i2gfZrLmb44jowAtv8EgQ/rLI7+fWjYfy76J\nZlKt9aMtDG76qbxxHuxH1iMJl9ovyQdyItQ9mJKOpVQcQALoUvWPS5DBMaftugvu\nJDgaDEmzeeb4o5688y29Gw8ecKgEnaFCtBmgF1/LVonFS/uHdhmXYgod3XRYVzTF\nCbxg3HnlcaL2pP5GAxj9eg/v2/ir2YtWoPSZoUQxTYT8dRI9bqo4BZZzNvldHAtn\nZNsl2iNXWLW9lciFFlRwDjz+ar4h8O43vcmT/3vlOHgViYJevl9UtvK5uk+MP82s\nOG+nFS0NcCezIPgMS/41M5ZXOHu3BQCu1Xcm1UP3skVMc0MV66F7j+2/VHlryfWw\nate2iADS8kPQggZzrHiKch3TgCIb5g9mRgoBAd06Z3EDTHJXaVD0nkXmhnNgmu5E\ne6GT1iJkRc64Hz1iKgkdz+GOC//our0lVbTKdmum6IQ6qIbg+kaIF0rafIcstaKA\nTlKPDS2gxaKH+IB9oXGHmZDwlwLuIjMfd5APKAgVz1eGyVlHbtZKcxrvIsfxjqeZ\ncgDKf06Y0Yuy3d8zk01W\n=h3NZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T12:32:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commit/43f051d07a31bad86e1e13f12924568ee28941d2","node_id":"C_kwDOP_6DBNoAKDQzZjA1MWQwN2EzMWJhZDg2ZTFlMTNmMTI5MjQ1NjhlZTI4OTQxZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commit/bba8e5462acd770e230bbecf6bd3939c0b17b5f5","sha":"bba8e5462acd770e230bbecf6bd3939c0b17b5f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/bba8e5462acd770e230bbecf6bd3939c0b17b5f5"}],"sha":"43f051d07a31bad86e1e13f12924568ee28941d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/43f051d07a31bad86e1e13f12924568ee28941d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232349910?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/VardAlb","id":232349910,"login":"VardAlb","node_id":"U_kgDODdlg1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/bba8e5462acd770e230bbecf6bd3939c0b17b5f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:27:34Z","email":"alberto.arpini@varda.ag","name":"VardAlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:27:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: sp-5584 add raster layer assets to raster export zip (#812)\n\n## Summary\nThe raster export job writes one raster output file per exported Raster\nLayer, but never included that layer''s Raster Layer Assets — auxiliary\nFiles (technical manuals, prediction layers, etc.) declared per Band in\na Band Mapping''s `additional_resources` and stored in\n`raster_layer_assets`. This closes that gap: for each Raster Layer whose\noutput is written to the export ZIP, its Raster Layer Assets are now\nfetched and added under a per-layer `assets/` subfolder.\n\nOut of scope: `Dataset.related_resources` (Dataset-level external URLs)\nis untouched — no changes to `Readme.pdf` or dataset-level metadata.\n\n## Changes\n- `SoilDataStorage`: new batch query to fetch Raster Layer Assets\n(joined with `files`) for a list of `raster_layer_id`s, grouped by\nlayer.\n- `exportHelpers.ts`: wrapper mirroring `fetchRasterLayers` for the new\nquery.\n- `RasterFileWriter`: `buildLayerName` made public; new method writes an\nasset buffer to `{tempDir}/assets/{layerName}/{sanitized filename}`,\ndisambiguating same-layer filename collisions.\n- `soilExportJob.ts`: after a layer''s raster output is written (`wrote\n=== true`), its assets are looked up, each unique File is read from\nstorage once (memoized per `file_id` for the job run), and written into\nevery referencing layer''s subfolder. A read failure on one asset is\nlogged as a warning and skipped — the export job never fails because of\nit.\n- Fixed accepted file formats for raster layer asset uploads (unrelated\nsmall fix surfaced during testing,\n`frontend/src/hooks/useAdditionalResourceUpload.ts`).\n\n## Design note\nA shared asset File attached to more than one exported layer is read\nfrom storage **once** but **written into every referencing layer''s own\nsubfolder**. The ZIP is not smaller in this case — each layer''s folder\nstays self-contained by design. Confirmed with the requester.\n\n## Tests\n- Unit tests for the new `SoilDataStorage` query, `RasterFileWriter`\nasset-writing method, and the upload hook fix.\n- Integration tests in `soilExportJob-integration.test.ts`: single-layer\nasset export, shared asset across two layers (storage read count\nasserted as 1), and missing/unreadable asset handling.","tree":{"sha":"f9c69c3e4c1052389f3fef171178d31cac60fb2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/trees/f9c69c3e4c1052389f3fef171178d31cac60fb2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/commits/bba8e5462acd770e230bbecf6bd3939c0b17b5f5","verification":{"payload":"tree f9c69c3e4c1052389f3fef171178d31cac60fb2a\nparent ae081e090fd71d7818eda219fc015c141f8e04e7\nauthor VardAlb <alberto.arpini@varda.ag> 1787920054 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787920054 +0200\n\nfeat: sp-5584 add raster layer assets to raster export zip (#812)\n\n## Summary\nThe raster export job writes one raster output file per exported Raster\nLayer, but never included that layer''s Raster Layer Assets — auxiliary\nFiles (technical manuals, prediction layers, etc.) declared per Band in\na Band Mapping''s `additional_resources` and stored in\n`raster_layer_assets`. This closes that gap: for each Raster Layer whose\noutput is written to the export ZIP, its Raster Layer Assets are now\nfetched and added under a per-layer `assets/` subfolder.\n\nOut of scope: `Dataset.related_resources` (Dataset-level external URLs)\nis untouched — no changes to `Readme.pdf` or dataset-level metadata.\n\n## Changes\n- `SoilDataStorage`: new batch query to fetch Raster Layer Assets\n(joined with `files`) for a list of `raster_layer_id`s, grouped by\nlayer.\n- `exportHelpers.ts`: wrapper mirroring `fetchRasterLayers` for the new\nquery.\n- `RasterFileWriter`: `buildLayerName` made public; new method writes an\nasset buffer to `{tempDir}/assets/{layerName}/{sanitized filename}`,\ndisambiguating same-layer filename collisions.\n- `soilExportJob.ts`: after a layer''s raster output is written (`wrote\n=== true`), its assets are looked up, each unique File is read from\nstorage once (memoized per `file_id` for the job run), and written into\nevery referencing layer''s subfolder. A read failure on one asset is\nlogged as a warning and skipped — the export job never fails because of\nit.\n- Fixed accepted file formats for raster layer asset uploads (unrelated\nsmall fix surfaced during testing,\n`frontend/src/hooks/useAdditionalResourceUpload.ts`).\n\n## Design note\nA shared asset File attached to more than one exported layer is read\nfrom storage **once** but **written into every referencing layer''s own\nsubfolder**. The ZIP is not smaller in this case — each layer''s folder\nstays self-contained by design. Confirmed with the requester.\n\n## Tests\n- Unit tests for the new `SoilDataStorage` query, `RasterFileWriter`\nasset-writing method, and the upload hook fix.\n- Integration tests in `soilExportJob-integration.test.ts`: single-layer\nasset export, shared asset across two layers (storage read count\nasserted as 1), and missing/unreadable asset handling.","rea