83875d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56585589?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/d-rom","id":56585589,"login":"d-rom","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NTg1NTg5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/d-rom","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/83687f6c59cd8bb30a8654ce3fec105d914a637d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:23:37Z","email":"daria.marassanova@varda.ag","name":"Daria Ruiz-Ogarrio Marassanova"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:23:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: filterRaster query optimization (#810)\n\nAll changes applied in rasterFilter function:\n- Merged 3 queries into one with CTEs, following the structure of the\nremaining soilDataStorage functions.\n- Replaced WHERE clauses `EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM aoi WHERE\nST_Intersects(rf.geom, aoi.geom))` and `EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM aoi WHERE\nrl.bbox && aoi.geom)` with JOINS to ensure raster_layer_footprints and\nuser_geometry_subdivisions spatial indexes are used.","tree":{"sha":"2f182346fada79efa9dc9eced7ae24eec05466f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/trees/2f182346fada79efa9dc9eced7ae24eec05466f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/commits/83687f6c59cd8bb30a8654ce3fec105d914a637d","verification":{"payload":"tree 2f182346fada79efa9dc9eced7ae24eec05466f9\nparent 8ae1d0da72482114162d07707628d17318e86ea7\nauthor Daria Ruiz-Ogarrio Marassanova <daria.marassanova@varda.ag> 1787840617 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787840617 +0200\n\nperf: filterRaster query optimization (#810)\n\nAll changes applied in rasterFilter function:\n- Merged 3 queries into one with CTEs, following the structure of the\nremaining soilDataStorage functions.\n- Replaced WHERE clauses `EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM aoi WHERE\nST_Intersects(rf.geom, aoi.geom))` and `EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM aoi WHERE\nrl.bbox && aoi.geom)` with JOINS to ensure raster_layer_footprints and\nuser_geometry_subdivisions spatial indexes are used.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkEhpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7nMQAE3j0uPfOL6ibFQ6dxyss8MA\nNeto5tn5PXmtID+V67xIh94luZmE45ZUFoP3g+aASPGILHTMdEWShMbLgyl16VYd\nLd5b9nlZ5b4ZIMKsTxxPDC+kYvu0Io3YFZK/lt/gKvWq/zUIydknAMMqcUHt0zlE\nwBjIRmeJCYAbo+zoOuhh6ASqKW0hZe1f5r2p9+pecbPBxc3X7f2kuxPYpmybAQQy\nzKLvENvssLluHrxo2aYODhpnXkXcG7PmveEbUWwEQlCFmDGj/EyT8SyfPIm2lQLT\ng8uxsYokpBd1Hx4PKkDwlCWmWx8vZPNEH62JpoP0UzYQlU5modIJjoOoHQzHAyoZ\n6vKmy0BeIEuao6goRtprHS6PkoCA7eA87KoAxRR+UtbTOVLxygDEwGTgcpqq+BY+\neMxYaYkde5R4QwXEhfVKLrBYkRrfKy3rpcKnmQyBN6OA9kuPJfTZDCMmZBMuaIpV\nHM6o3DGeTxvWybPvywdd8RxwyFAqHpfPHRFB7FHnuTlY6xdIGYCKmAzgSJf1qkIX\nEijfWQ/hbB5LD0HtRlx5LIoL1JYQhh/FZpxJ5qHRAdMqFktWFJWGZDg73KUX/xNQ\ndNp0On29BEQ+8IrsIbmDIv5byWin12A7lJb5nG/eYypt4HWt4uJlQf5mn6o8w0h2\n6WcRyRMA38UGTPFFPHLI\n=qI9B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T14:23:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commit/83687f6c59cd8bb30a8654ce3fec105d914a637d","node_id":"C_kwDOP_6DBNoAKDgzNjg3ZjZjNTljZDhiYjMwYTg2NTRjZTNmZWMxMDVkOTE0YTYzN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commit/8ae1d0da72482114162d07707628d17318e86ea7","sha":"8ae1d0da72482114162d07707628d17318e86ea7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/8ae1d0da72482114162d07707628d17318e86ea7"}],"sha":"83687f6c59cd8bb30a8654ce3fec105d914a637d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/83687f6c59cd8bb30a8654ce3fec105d914a637d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/232349910?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/VardAlb","id":232349910,"login":"VardAlb","node_id":"U_kgDODdlg1g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VardAlb","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/commits/8ae1d0da72482114162d07707628d17318e86ea7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:51:34Z","email":"alberto.arpini@varda.ag","name":"VardAlb"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T11:51:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: sp-5587 limit max upload size via config (#808)\n\n## Summary\nAdd a configurable maximum upload size for the ingestion and logo upload\nflows.\n\n- `MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE_MB` env var (default 500 when unset).\n- Public `GET /storage/config` endpoint, mirroring\n`ConfigService.getAuthConfig()`''s pattern: returns `storageMode` and\n`maxUploadSizeMB` only, never S3 credentials.\n- Enforcement at two layers: an early `Content-Type:\nmultipart/form-data` + `Content-Length` gate, and multer''s `fileSize`\nlimit as the authoritative check. Both paths return `413` with a\n`problemDetails` body.\n- Frontend `useStorageConfig` hook, consumed by the three upload\nsurfaces (soil data, additional resources, logo upload) to show the\nlimit in human-readable units and reject oversized files client-side\nbefore any network call.\n\n## Scope\n- One shared limit across `/files` and `/frontend/logo` (see ADR-0029) —\nno per-route limits.\n- `GET /storage/config` is public, matching `/auth/config`.\n- `JSON_PAYLOAD_LIMIT` behavior is unchanged.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"085b433bd9c41b1634b69f5865b9105331c086fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/trees/085b433bd9c41b1634b69f5865b9105331c086fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/commits/8ae1d0da72482114162d07707628d17318e86ea7","verification":{"payload":"tree 085b433bd9c41b1634b69f5865b9105331c086fc\nparent 13b5e42bdbb6fce8f4bd65a3879f5a34849787dd\nauthor VardAlb <alberto.arpini@varda.ag> 1787745094 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787745094 +0200\n\nfeat: sp-5587 limit max upload size via config (#808)\n\n## Summary\nAdd a configurable maximum upload size for the ingestion and logo upload\nflows.\n\n- `MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE_MB` env var (default 500 when unset).\n- Public `GET /storage/config` endpoint, mirroring\n`ConfigService.getAuthConfig()`''s pattern: returns `storageMode` and\n`maxUploadSizeMB` only, never S3 credentials.\n- Enforcement at two layers: an early `Content-Type:\nmultipart/form-data` + `Content-Length` gate, and multer''s `fileSize`\nlimit as the authoritative check. Both paths return `413` with a\n`problemDetails` body.\n- Frontend `useStorageConfig` hook, consumed by the three upload\nsurfaces (soil data, additional resources, logo upload) to show the\nlimit in human-readable units and reject oversized files client-side\nbefore any network call.\n\n## Scope\n- One shared limit across `/files` and `/frontend/logo` (see ADR-0029) —\nno per-route limits.\n- `GET /storage/config` is public, matching `/auth/config`.\n- `JSON_PAYLOAD_LIMIT` behavior is unchanged.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjtNGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfKAQAHdiLGifjHrGzd5ufJ2TkHb0\nisfx7FZ4tJiD384VWRKi/Ri03PmHK9BOrk3v/gSfKrAuJAIvhSMYt1eFJpFJ/Y20\n06ZrS49dZbKxQrgStPqGhJjC4SXipGenT+Ua7163KN9EZEG1Qo2Rez5jeJh3PD3d\n/pOZgdxp2EC9Db524ulZ5Kkfpw4AYn/XE0V06P6oryNxjyOwDavZCgE9qfHUszw9\nwNE81CSdzaPKgNKc40+zmjeydw/s2PZAmFPpO0d/kkXUsfymnGFYSQ47XnmNIZVL\ncyoRfQAu1O0Nw/vc55wCybR4TJtyUTDBailYV5U3v67ZQq+dBC6sdADQeRyOv3m1\nZKzV3/ceRWDbEpgKwqOLSwHSYGmG4idWyjBeJGW0TKY/M+0PCPU/aNpGSE2A5chY\nhXtdJ4+jEJG2dq9M+4dvTDyhR3dB14zwkLBNiwZSw9vHBPlV5+N1RI23ZL7hvsWN\nThmNzsbPLdg3ma6oOEBDHWd3gNejxZWgUoms8oAyJWwZS+ZGE/VNqL2pJmlXkArh\nrS1vt8cScfqjDyVnuLmI1HN41GEZ0jGAkpabVVjlAagxTBFYuOSqAZsgqjcplvCB\nvqvd7IeWy+nm9Upqu/w