ch relies on\n`entitlements`, passed by the `auth` middleware. In this case, though,\n`DOWNLOAD` and `PREVIEW` capabilities are hardcoded when needed as the\nlist of datasets is now","tree":{"sha":"73cf02c89d632bdeb14aa808c31733ba27d52d71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/trees/73cf02c89d632bdeb14aa808c31733ba27d52d71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/varda-ag/soilhive-core/git/commits/4d4e602c40d66d6f6fa69156a2f89de0f96903e9","verification":{"payload":"tree 73cf02c89d632bdeb14aa808c31733ba27d52d71\nparent 68a5174ef24cb02dc70282429c76e4d2d8aaaa45\nauthor VardAlb <alberto.arpini@varda.ag> 1787320753 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787320753 +0200\n\nfeat: sp-5560 filter and coverage dataset listings expose per-dataset capabilities (#796)\n\n- added new function `expandAcrossSlugHistory` to resolve multiple slugs\nin a single db round trip (instead of using existing function\n`resolveSlugs` which works with a single slug at a time):\nhttps://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/blob/f7e59d52c6f784ad69f4c9198d469a128968cfd2/backend/src/services/EntitlementService.ts#L135\n- used this new function in `getUserEntitlements` that is, in turn, used\nby `GET /entitlements`. Entitlements are now returned as expanded across\nall slugs:\n```\n{\n    \"sample-kenya-3\": [\n        \"preview\"\n    ],\n    \"sample-kenya-alberto\": [\n        \"preview\"\n    ]\n}\n```\n> [!NOTE]\n> `GET /entitlements` doesn''t return capabilities for data-admins and\nuser admins as this would imply loading all datasets. Frontend need to\nenforce this logic in its `useEntitlements` hook\n- frontend hook `useEntitlements` read user entitlements at startup:\nhttps://github.com/varda-ag/soilhive-core/blob/b803af4eff8e10da8c2ad2f8023b5bb1a3b299da/frontend/src/hooks/useEntitlementsHook.ts#L67\n- `useEntitlements` `can` function is used across the frontend to\ndisplay the datasets list and the ''Explore'' and ''Download'' buttons\n- backend `DatasetService` 