","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDQ3MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/commits/5486b7ff5f615022c11822310d1f00ea57a61fb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:00:13Z","email":"65047246+Kinfe123@users.noreply.github.com","name":"KinfeMichael Tariku"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:00:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(schema): destructive migration steps behind --allow-destructive (#1843)\n\ndropColumn and dropTable steps delete data, so:\n\n- they never run without --allow-destructive on top of --apply; the run\n  stops at the first one, later steps wait, and the terminal prompt cannot\n  skip it\n- farm only drops what it recorded the plugin creating: a column the app\n  added to a plugin''s table, a table another plugin creates, or a table\n  the plugin only describes is never dropped; the run stops and says why\n- a step cannot drop something the plugin still declares (fails when the\n  config loads)\n- an already-dropped column or table is only recorded; fresh installs run\n  nothing\n\nalso fixes the version snapshot moving forward while steps are still\npending: a refused drop left no record of what the plugin created, so the\ndrop could never run afterwards.","tree":{"sha":"67e4517c04757eac0701191674916ae56633e37f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/git/trees/67e4517c04757eac0701191674916ae56633e37f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/git/commits/5486b7ff5f615022c1182231