the ALTER TABLE commented out with the entry\n  to add; --apply creates the plugin''s own tables, adds only allowed columns,\n  and exits 1 while any are missing. existing columns are never changed\n- in a project with prisma/schema.prisma or a drizzle config, the app''s\n  tables are never altered: migrate and generate --orm print the line to add\n- farm schema check reports missing tables and columns, type mismatches,\n  and two plugins adding the same column\n- sync folds the app''s own extend into its models first, so nothing changes\n  for sync\n\n* test(schema): compare only this file''s tables in the read-only check test\n\nthe postgres ci job runs the schema test files in parallel against one\ndatabase. the read-only test snapshotted every table in the schema, so a\ntable another file created mid-test (schema-extend''s) looked like the check\nwriting. reproduced by creating unrelated tables during the test; scoped to\nthe farm_check_ tables this file creates, and still fails when the check\nwrites.","tree":{"sha":"72cb4e67100a0b78be2e312a92409237e6131b4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/git/trees/72cb4e67100a0b78be2e312a92409237e6131b4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/git/commits/7c70ee7eeb41079128a76a33115f0b1d75ddce55","verification":{"payload":"tree 72cb4e67100a0b78be2e312a92409237e6131b4f\nparent d85045df3c7a7c912e6673cfb20564a2844de230\nauthor KinfeMichael Tariku <65047246+Kinfe123@users.noreply.github.com> 1791240311 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791240311 -0700\n\nfeat(schema): let plugins add columns to the app''s tables, with the app''s approval (#1759)\n\n* feat(schema): let plugins add columns to the app''s tables, with the app''s approval\n\n- extend on an external model asks for columns on a table the plugin does\n  not own. each must be nullable or have a default; unique, indexed and\n  primary-key columns are rejected while the config loads\n- the app allows it with schema: { allowExtend: { loyalty: [\"user\"] } }\n  in farm.config, by model or table name\n- farm <plugin> migrate prints the ALTER TABLE commented out with the entry\n  to add; --apply creates the plugin''s own tables, adds only allowed columns,\n  and exits 1 while any are missing. existing columns are never changed\n- in a project with prisma/schema.prisma or a drizzle config, the app''s\n  tables are never altered: migrate and generate --orm print the line to add\n- farm schema check reports missing tables and columns, type mismatches,\n  and two plugins adding the same column\n- sync folds the app''s own extend into its models first, so nothing changes\n  for sync\n\n* test(schema): compare only this file''s tables in the read-only check test\n\nthe postgres ci job runs the schema test files in parallel against one\ndatabase. the read-only test snapshotted every table in the schema, so a\ntable another file created mid-test (schema-extend''s) looked like the check\nwriting. reproduced by creating unrelated tables during the test; scoped to\nthe farm_check_ tables this file creates, and still fails when the check\nwrites.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxCh3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhcwQAGeNFQ3/2d8KlEeLObvIpKee\nGgCeZiAjVVi5debnK+Ahi8QMiU/JqnciOzDnJqxg8ciG//Zm+6wmEXJz+ZtLYDRZ\nlgtvRONJKb6xayxNfdsFM+ZfGksCYPz4c+AF9i5IN2p9HnYqQPhARWMzBu1O/N8x\n0WXrrHhxpzId8mi8XpRS+As9tVBw/nSjdX0u7qJ4OeIz6BSw+mNwMeDMVshK1tHb\ngLP210du2/koXgt202sgivzsZj6RutBFTo+TokLsIkp0yRJGzhG1xy6ngVa7qmvI\nlbkb8kOYaMoPFIH/qpVPypbQHfezBoB8Hcv12k7jorAvXrTT35591XaWlgmwJ1M2\nRdBOj/8/6Jv/bzTucXidUFpIHiOOU8UOb3z3CZFIHzTH1GAYPezeHmyAv2r9Fv47\nJU7Zz1fNCwjIiHjxas6XgPp9XB9opir2L2m1v2LNfEpR6b6XT9IKb2gUHjIgqDlK\nlHj4Erltsbe9cLNYvctbg/cjkl/YSexxjO+MXOZ8OHlxnAoK6KCBes3e+5bqkLf2\nX1ay5qvVnVfJzw+GN5wjeECASD+s1ofETXCHN36gR7+512nTy5kPDz2pgbW+QT/2\nYirG+Ytqy0bAJH4cdrXL48v4iNSAsejMrb+uv1qS6gfX3nXHeTVIAywydlS4jIPo\nNwA+Wbck4BdcHyo5bzsD\n=ZaMm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true