bs/farm.js/commits/c193e7abb62b09a4323d42dd28fa45fbe2fea3f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:39:07Z","email":"65047246+Kinfe123@users.noreply.github.com","name":"KinfeMichael Tariku"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:39:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(docs): keep the agents figures from shifting the page or animating off screen (#1754)\n\nReadouts reserve their lines, one where the longest fits and two where a\nfigure is narrower, so the page below no longer jumps as they change on\nphones and mid-width screens. Fig 4''s longest readout is shortened to fit.\n\nFig 3''s keystroke pulse follows the scene''s clock instead of an endless\nCSS animation, which kept running off screen from the first load.\n\nOn touch screens a tap keeps its explanation (a touch pointer leaves when\nthe finger lifts), and closing the close-up lets the scene play on.","tree":{"sha":"07046f2a629a5327c67fc73d9fc74edc802bc5df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/git/trees/07046f2a629a5327c67fc73d9fc74edc802bc5df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/git/commits/c193e7abb62b09a4323d42dd28fa45fbe2fea3f5","verification":{"payload":"tree 07046f2a629a5327c67fc73d9fc74edc802bc5df\nparent d27480728735bb442bba7dfa89dcca53672a655f\nauthor KinfeMichael Tariku <65047246+Kinfe123@users.noreply.github.com> 1791236347 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791236347 -0700\n\nfix(docs): keep the agents figures from shifting the page or animating off screen (#1754)\n\nReadouts reserve their lines, one where the longest fits and two where a\nfigure is narrower, so the page below no longer jumps as they change on\nphones and mid-width screens. Fig 4''s longest readout is shortened to fit.\n\nFig 3''s keystroke pulse follows the scene''s clock instead of an endless\nCSS animation, which kept running off screen from the first load.\n\nOn touch screens a tap keeps its explanation (a touch pointer leaves when\nthe finger lifts), and closing the close-up lets the scene play on.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxBj7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAok8QABhIGPihvHwjtTgT/7ybrrnw\nfjha9TjjyDVR3d9FU8MhHZpLgB9HkFNDajld9kpap/4FTbsz70d1WDoWpYO9H7nH\nI9EDA1odh7v4vZFwuuuw5FcVj7CjaUGfKwgY2NAlQb4hOkwzx0AN83FRP+i847Ta\nYESKcGYZaJE+o/8djh9e7C909AqNSq0voja3VdEdtKAYhtzeM/DY6bHwBv2RewJi\nFanL+UuPvTzhhJWS05C3IVq9rHf7y2LgHbkllPuVPlJkpiv/ewZ+lCuej5/ZaWec\nUtp8eped6xM8e4wYwXOycVPCwlgTwnY5wV9oz3GhL9vG94nsSuCd9WrRms3ohGRo\n8B6pVaGOZVAYnLCwCRKTbl8i2KdNkJxOQ9ahBZncTpP2eavy8sl08j/KPz15+A8y\nwid5qxmoTeiZb5XujMhgTjeQ4NSaS/nvNvVL8ODUMVFQd67v1U1Lfx3QUGzUW6PM\nQxqSWwjC4oyzNLiJ9NEfd91B3sq//s7+fy7vLIdxsYRl/ss8vlgNhKPRNwA+qVWo\nSH4cJZmI9j9FstOev1jWbqVQtGauOD/Lp+baFTt1S+/15sTJAr3mXnxvBZ2t1XRN\n0nBHwU5y7yM/+Z1/Z4Ny9Gyz+StadNi+cHppBWzXbEH9egYuDb6PM38ET64qTi2h\n7W8GZJjxwElWu/H5f0qr\n=uIy6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T21:39:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/farming-labs/farm.js/commit/c193e7abb62b09a4323d42dd28fa45fbe2fea3f5","node_id":"C_kwDOQAkI0toAKGMxOTNlN2FiYjYyYjA5YTQzMjNkNDJkZDI4ZmE0NWZiZTJmZWEzZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/farming-labs/farm.js/commit/d27480728735bb442bba7dfa89dcca53672a655f","sha":"d27480728735bb442bba7dfa89dcca53672a655f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/commits/d27480728735bb442bba7dfa89dcca53672a655f"}],"sha":"c193e7abb62b09a4323d42dd28fa45fbe2fea3f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/commits/c193e7abb62b09a4323d42dd28fa45fbe2fea3f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65047246?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Kinfe123","id":65047246,"login":"Kinfe123","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDQ3MjQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kinfe123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/commits/d27480728735bb442bba7dfa89dcca53672a655f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:13:41Z","email":"65047246+Kinfe123@users.noreply.github.com","name":"KinfeMichael Tariku"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T21:13:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(plugin): declare tables with definePlugin({ schema }) and let apps rename them (#1741)\n\n* feat(plugin): declare tables with definePlugin({ schema }) and let apps rename them\n\n- definePlugin({ schema }) registers the plugin''s tables: farm <name> migrate\n  (from the plugin name), farm generate, and farm schema check, reached through\n  the app''s storage.client. the schema is validated while the config loads\n- external: true marks a model the plugin uses but never creates, such as the\n  app''s user table; migrate, orm generation, foreign keys and conflict checks\n  skip it while references and queries still resolve its real name\n- renameSchema + FarmSchemaRenames<typeof schema> let an app point a plugin at\n  its own table and column names, typed from the plugin''s schema\n- farm schema check reports two plugins declaring tables under one name\n\n* fix(schema): name the real table in comments for references to external models\n\nmigrate, prisma, drizzle and mongo output printed the schema''s model and\nfield keys (user.id) for a reference to a model the owner describes but\ndoes not create. after an app renames it, that pointed at a table that\ndoes not exist. collectSchemaModels now records the real target and every\nrenderer prints it (members_auth.user_id).\n\n* docs(plugins): wrap the renameSchema example so it fits the code block\n\n* feat(plugin): definePlugin({ database }) and keep declareSchemaTables internal\n\nplugin authors declare tables only through definePlugin. database: { client,\ndialect? } covers the one case the docs still sent them to declareSchemaTables\nfor: tables kept outside storage.client. declareSchemaTables stays exported\nfor farm''s own packages and earlier betas, marked @internal, and is gone from\nthe docs, error hints and examples.\n\n* refactor(sync): declare tables through definePlugin and forward the app''s database\n\nsync now uses definePlugin({ schema, database }) instead of the internal\ndeclaration: models the app did not expose are external, and database\nforwards the client or storage mount the app passed to sync(). behaviour is\nunchanged: same command, same tables, same no-data-source error.\n\ndatabase.client left undefined falls back to storage.client, so a plugin\nforwards an optional app setting without a conditional. definePlugin also\nlists owned model keys on the declaration, which older cores read, and sync\nmodel types skip external models.","tree":{"sha":"f39bfe162d2c51c1bb1029095c069ba18bc6237d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/git/trees/f39bfe162d2c51c1bb1029095c069ba18bc6237d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/farming-labs/farm.js/git/commits/d27480728735bb442bba7dfa89dcca53672a655f","verification":{"payload":"tree f39bfe162d2c51c1bb1029095c069ba18bc6237d\nparent 36ec60bbbc66185f8014a870dea5a1cef2442b9c\nauthor KinfeMichael Tariku <65047246+Kinfe123@users.noreply.github.com> 1791234821 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791234821 -0700\n\nfeat(plugin): declare tables with definePlugin({ schema }) and let apps rename them (#1741)\n\n* feat(plugin): declare tables with definePlugin({ schema }) and let apps rename them\n\n- definePlugin({ schema }) registers the plugin''s tables: farm <name> migrate\n  (from the plugin name), farm generate, and farm schema check, reached through\n  the app''s storage.client. the schema is validated while the config loads\n- external: true marks a model the plugin uses but never creates, such as the\n  app''s user table; migrate, orm generation, foreign keys and conflict checks\n  skip it while references and queries still resolve its real name\n- renameSchema + FarmSchemaRenames<typeof schema> let an app point a plugin at\n  its own table and column names, typed from the plugin''s schema\n- farm schema check reports two plugins declaring tables under one name\n\n* fix(schema): name the real table in comments for references to external models\n\nmigrate, prisma, drizzle and mongo output printed the schema''s model and\nfield keys (user.id) for a reference to a model the owner describes but\ndoes not create. after an app renames it, that pointed at a table that\ndoes not exist. collectSchemaModels now records the real target and every\nrenderer prints it (members_auth.user_id).\n\n* docs(plugins): wrap the renameSchema example so it fits the code block\n\n* feat(plugin): definePlugin({ database }) and keep declareSchemaTables internal\n\nplugin authors declare tables only through definePlugin. database: { client,\ndialect? } covers the one case the docs still sent them to declareSchemaTables\nfor: tables kept outside storage.client. declareSchemaTables stays exported\nfor farm''s own packages and earlier betas, marked @internal, and is gone from\nthe docs, error hints and examples.\n\n* refactor(sync): declare tables through definePlugin and forward the app''s database\n\nsync now uses definePlugin({ schema, database }) instead of the internal\ndeclaration: models the app did not expose are external, and database\nforwards the client or storage mount the app passed to sync(). behaviour is\nunchanged: same command, same tables, same no-data-source error.\n\ndatabase.client left undefined falls back to storage.client, so a plugin\nforwards an optional app setting without a conditional. definePlugin also\nlists owned model keys on the declaration, which older cores read, and sync\nmodel types skip external models.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxBMFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC0MQAE1LvnVGpIesKpJgWPW26fYG\nqrQAmGIUYEYKYTPTLSKNl49zSAriC2pcnn5dZYblgkFegSHrK8oh0915JmdpOi5P\nOP5QM2hsdzzc6UPthujzl5b2Z8u4KE7bpbo8r2XgV3iwpDy6mIIUzTu7DZN7kW97\nNDJ440ReJpdef5Ry2KPft2aw6JhdJplFlEfLm4GRAYxw45Cb99LBkj7dh/oUYOU7\nZ0Xj9U0oceounUqdlUXTBZd55NknDuNPnrM3ZtostLXNtT2J4eMBLqLro6VR81w8\nsopE2KWwlRAiK5/TjGTKUzXbFJPeDVRDR3NpgoAymL5+I6280L2KgWyhch7Bjk3B\nqu8qH6ImtZu9N2lCqPAV2pJWcDLdtFZno+rrMRAMYcb826fSQeiJI37+pnEy6CR9\nhtcpnTRALxgljMR//DO0Ysa0Tcnl4gFAQ+nvHj/RaMdVAVonQKYQUj7k8LN3fncW\nGQSZYVNsxTTnGtnJi/KLf1Yjt0hk/SrnIGQuTJBRZYUset6XH13FrDhhtg1JM8Pm\nXqf6vSWhqs43kapX+B37XyIvX65lV