.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/38491049c1e3e7d546a4c06b946ab129bb447e03"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/abe4eaa17a8977134053b29d8eb8510ce99553f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T06:40:56Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T06:40:56Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"docs: give the source tree a rule and the bundle an enforced budget\n\nThe source-tree listing had become an exhaustive mirror for three\ndirectories and an elided sketch for the rest, with no stated rule and two\ncounts that had already drifted from what src/conversions holds. It now\nstates what it lists and why, names each module''s role in one line, and\nleaves the counts to the gate that checks them. Module descriptions live in\nCLAUDE.md alone rather than in a shorter second copy here, and CLAUDE.md\ngains the three utility modules the tree listed and it did not.\n\nThe plugin bundle size was recorded as an exact byte count measured by hand,\nbeside a size-limit budget that CI actually enforces. The enforced figure is\nthe one recorded now, so it cannot go stale.\n\nThe theme paragraph claimed the browser check asserts the stored preference\nvalues against the root theme attribute, while saying two sentences earlier\nthat the host-following default writes no attribute at all. It now says what\nthe check asserts, and the note on writing the placement out gives the\nreason that holds: it is a convention shared across these panels, not\nprotection against a title the shell would resolve anyway.\n\nThe README described the theme selector twice. The feature bullet names the\ncontrols and their themes; what each automatic choice follows moved to the\npanel-area entry that already described the selector.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TrhyiHJbhmfXmLpqFFzeEY","tree":{"sha":"f39c4b6a21dd1ee640c9a46792eb2c7b77f0e63f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/f39c4b6a21dd1ee640c9a46792eb2c7b77f0e63f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/abe4eaa17a8977134053b29d8eb8510ce99553f7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https