url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/ccf535d569283df7ab6759539a25a3ba76d87a78/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T04:10:05Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T04:10:05Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"chore: update shared UI to 0.11.1\n\nThe theme selector names its two automatic choices for what they follow:\nMatch Admin replaces Auto and follows the Signal K Admin theme, showing\nLight where the host sets none, and Match device replaces System and\nfollows the operating system preference. Both keep their stored values,\n`auto` and `system`, so a saved preference survives the rename. The\nselector also carries its own group label and a line saying what Match\nAdmin follows, so the two no longer read as one offer written twice.\n\nThe save bar refuses a blocked save through `aria-disabled` rather than\nthe native attribute, so Save and Discard keep their place in the tab\norder while a validation error blocks saving. Its status copy reads \"All\nchanges saved\", \"Save to enable the plugin\", and \"Save sent to the\nserver\", which is what the browser check now waits for after a save.\n\nEvery field, group, checkbox, radio group, and segmented-control error\nleads with a danger tone mark and a spoken tone word, a focused number\nfield gives up focus before a wheel or trackpad scroll can spin its\nvalue, and ages a day and older are counted in numbers.\n\nRegenerates the third-party notices against the new version and moves the\nCHANGELOG entry, the README, and the architecture notes with it. The\npanel size baseline is re-recorded at 96,063 gzip bytes, because the\nrelease folds in the shared primitives the consumer panels had each\nwritten for themselves and this panel bundles the library.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TrhyiHJbhmfXmLpqFFzeEY","tree":{"sha":"fea5149b3194d0179fdaf90d5a49f1452503f97c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/fea5149b3194d0179fdaf90d5a49f1452503f97c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/ccf535d569283df7ab6759539a25a3ba76d87a78","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/ccf535d569283df7ab6759539a25a3ba76d87a78","node_id":"C_kwDOQApVMtoAKGNjZjUzNWQ1NjkyODNkZjdhYjY3NTk1MzlhMjVhM2JhNzZkODdhNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/e911704824fac7098a364d0e2a7f8d4bfc81922d","sha":"e911704824fac7098a364d0e2a7f8d4bfc81922d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/e911704824fac7098a364d0e2a7f8d4bfc81922d"}],"sha":"ccf535d569283df7ab6759539a25a3ba76d87a78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/ccf535d569283df7ab6759539a25a3ba76d87a78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/e911704824fac7098a364d0e2a7f8d4bfc81922d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:36:43Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:41:00Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"docs: prepare 1.11.0\n\nThe entry is built from the diff rather than from summaries, which is\nwhat caught the whole range-guard batch, the detached writer detection,\nand the advisor schedule gate: none of them appeared in the staged\nentry. The Fixed section sorts by failure mode, because whether a field\nwraps or drops is the distinction a new conversion has to get right.\n\nTroubleshooting gained the two cases where a blank field is not a\nmistake to chase: a shaft turning astern legitimately blanks engine\nspeed, since Signal K permits a negative revolutions and the wire field\nis unsigned, and an angle never blanks at all because it wraps, so a\nunit mistake there shows as a wrong direction rather than a missing\nvalue. The unit checklist gained pressures, trim state, depth and heave\nin metres, engine revolutions in hertz, and rate of turn in radians per\nsecond.\n\nCLAUDE.md records the wrap-versus-drop rule and adds the unsigned angle\nceiling to the constants that must not be corrected upward, because\n6.2831 reads as a typo for a full turn until you know why it is not.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"831f0906214ac102be7b2096a1a21fc078cab4e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/831f0906214ac102be7b2096a1a21fc078cab4e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/e911704824fac7098a364d0e2a7f8d4bfc81922d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/e911704824fac7098a364d0e2a7f8d4bfc81922d","node_id":"C_kwDOQApVMtoAKGU5MTE3MDQ4MjRmYWM3MDk4YTM2NGQwZTJhN2Y4ZDRiZmM4MTkyMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/b44854923ea48724b50eecb487eb6db17ebfbb6f","sha":"b44854923ea48724b50eecb487eb6db17ebfbb6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/b44854923ea48724b50eecb487eb6db17ebfbb6f"}],"sha":"e911704824fac7098a364d0e2a7f8d4bfc81922d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/e911704824fac7098a364d0e2a7f8d4bfc81922d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/b44854923ea48724b50eecb487eb6db17ebfbb6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:36:20Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:36:20Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(panel): keep focus and announcements where the user can follow them\n\nThree controls removed themselves from under the user''s own focus,\ndropping a keyboard or screen reader user on the document body with no\nroute back. Two are Retry buttons whose hook clears its error only on\nsuccess, so a retry that works unmounts the banner the button is in; the\nthird is the toolbar Clear button, which empties the search that renders\nit. Each now hands focus on as it goes: the publisher select the retry\njust filled, the search box, and the search box again.\n\nThree announcing regions never announced. Each was built inside the\nconditional that produced its first message, so the region arrived\nalready carrying its text and nothing changed for a screen reader to\nnotice: the search result count, the setup wizard''s scan status, and a\nstatus chip. Each is mounted now and empties instead of unmounting.\n\nPressing Enable all twice said nothing, because an identical string is\nnot a change a live region reports. The apply counter is the announce\nkey now, which is also what retires a zero-width space padded onto the\nmessage to force a repeat.\n\nThe NMEA 2000 output state was read out twice, by a metric and a toolbar\nchip carrying the same value. The toolbar chip is the single announcer:\nit is never conditional and never inside a hidden container.\n\nSmooth scrolling ignored a reduced-motion preference on both jump\nhandlers, which is the only motion the panel produces. A validation jump\nalso scrolled twice, because moving focus re-scrolled and undid the\nplacement the jump had just made.\n\nTabs are generic over the category type, so a typo is a compile error\nrather than an inferred literal, and the guard that narrowed a reported\nvalue back is gone. A tab panel builds its content only where it renders\nit. A row''s disclosure ids come from the library rather than a DOM query\nover aria-expanded.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"5eaaee139f5fc9cc2be407a227af61ce3813dc10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/5eaaee139f5fc9cc2be407a227af61ce3813dc10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/b44854923ea48724b50eecb487eb6db17ebfbb6f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/b44854923ea48724b50eecb487eb6db17ebfbb6f","node_id":"C_kwDOQApVMtoAKGI0NDg1NDkyM2VhNDg3MjRiNTBlZWNiNDg3ZWI2ZGIxN2ViZmJiNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/3acf785eb421d036eb54defd2e4acc9e9cb129ad","sha":"3acf785eb421d036eb54defd2e4acc9e9cb129ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/3acf785eb421d036eb54defd2e4acc9e9cb129ad"}],"sha":"b44854923ea48724b50eecb487eb6db17ebfbb6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/b44854923ea48724b50eecb487eb6db17ebfbb6f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/3acf785eb421d036eb54defd2e4acc9e9cb129ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:35:52Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:35:52Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix(conversions): bound six fields that wrapped or overflowed on the wire\n\nEach of these put a wrong value on the NMEA 2000 bus rather than no\nvalue, which is worse, because a receiver cannot tell a wrapped reading\nfrom a real one. Every case below was measured by encoding and decoding\nthrough canboat rather than read off the field definition.\n\nPGN 128000 leeway had no guard, alone among the signed angle fields. A\nprovider publishing degrees sends 5, which reaches the receiver as\n-1.5536 radians, so five degrees of crab to starboard displays as\neighty-nine degrees to port.\n\nPGN 127251 rate of turn wrapped with a sign change: 100 rad/s reaches\nthe receiver as -34.2 rad/s, so a starboard swing is reported to every\nautopilot on the bus as a port one. A provider publishing degrees per\nminute lands exactly there.\n\nPGN 127252 heave wrapped the same way: a provider publishing\nmillimetres sends -400 for a drop into a trough, which arrives as a rise\nof 255 metres.\n\nPGN 127493 transmission oil pressure and temperature had no guard,\nunlike their PGN 127489 namesakes. A gearbox sender publishing Celsius\nsends -5, which arrives as 6548.6 K, and a failing pressure sender\narrives as 64 bar.\n\nPGN 128267 depth was guarded at the shallow end only, though its comment\nclaimed both.\n\nUnsigned angles gained the bound their signed counterparts already had.\nThe decoder discards any raw value above the field ceiling, and for the\n0.0001 radian field the last 0.005 degrees below north round onto it, so\na heading of 359.999 degrees arrived as not-available. Normalizing into\nzero to two pi does not avoid that band, because the band sits at the\ntop of the interval. This is the one bound in the release that alters a\nvalue rather than dropping it, by at most 0.005 degrees.\n\nNine round-trip regression cases, each verified to fail with its own\nguard reverted. The rudder case now uses Math.PI, which is the input\nthat discriminates: a value past pi was rejected by the old bound too\nand proved nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"d40682bd93620eaa2018445e66faebb42ff68f43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/d40682bd93620eaa2018445e66faebb42ff68f43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/3acf785eb421d036eb54defd2e4acc9e9cb129ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/3acf785eb421d036eb54defd2e4acc9e9cb129ad","node_id":"C_kwDOQApVMtoAKDNhY2Y3ODVlYjQyMWQwMzZlYjU0ZGVmZDJlNGFjYzllOWNiMTI5YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/bd210bf422a0b365fc3c39b7e0a315dd115e7cd0","sha":"bd210bf422a0b365fc3c39b7e0a315dd115e7cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/bd210bf422a0b365fc3c39b7e0a315dd115e7cd0"}],"sha":"3acf785eb421d036eb54defd2e4acc9e9cb129ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/3acf785eb421d036eb54defd2e4acc9e9cb129ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/bd210bf422a0b365fc3c39b7e0a315dd115e7cd0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:35:22Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T20:35:22Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"build: bring dependencies current and delete the local panel harness\n\nThe shared UI pin moves to 0.10.1 and biome to 2.5.13, with biome.json''s\nschema reference brought back in step with the installed version.\n\ntest:panel now runs the library''s own --runtime mode instead of a local\nnode:vm harness, and scripts/check-panel-runtime.mjs is deleted. The old\nharness asserted the literal string a browser without CSS @scope is\nshown, which is the library''s copy hand-mirrored into this repository.\nThe library matches its own attribute instead, so a wording change\nupstream can no longer break this gate. The --expect anchor is a string\nthe browser check already asserts, so both share one contract rather\nthan coupling to panel copy twice.\n\nFour action pin comments named the wrong release, one of them a major:\nthe setup-go pin is v7.0.0 and was labelled v6.0.0, and two checkout\npins are v7.0.1 and were labelled v7.0.0. Six floating comments now name\nthe exact release. zizmor-action moves to v0.6.4, verified clean by\nrunning the scanner it bundles against these workflows.\n\nThe packaging gate rejects prepare, postinstall, and preinstall, which\nnpm 10 executes during a pack that asks it not to.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018aSp3UBmuk7sCWP62Roags","tree":{"sha":"adfe13ec0c01d63ce72377017573b34e8080e0b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/adfe13ec0c01d63ce72377017573b34e8080e0b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/bd210bf422a0b365fc3c39b7e0a315dd115e7cd0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://ap