","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/5764190ecedfa0f2ef4686c528448e2f17a78a98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:28:59Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:28:59Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"build: assert the shared UI pin from one place\n\ncheck-package.mjs held a third copy of the shared UI version constant and its\ntwo assertions, so a bump had to be made in three files or the release gate\nfailed after the panel checks had already passed. All three now call the shared\nhelper.\n\nAlso names the PGN 129029 satellite-count ceiling for what it is. It shares the\nvalue 252 with the instance ceiling, but it is a different field and reusing\nthat constant read as if the two were related.","tree":{"sha":"e69dc099d182098663a6f9e59a798010baa1a60a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/e69dc099d182098663a6f9e59a798010baa1a60a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/5764190ecedfa0f2ef4686c528448e2f17a78a98","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/5764190ecedfa0f2ef4686c528448e2f17a78a98","node_id":"C_kwDOQApVMtoAKDU3NjQxOTBlY2VkZmEwZjJlZjQ2ODZjNTI4NDQ4ZTJmMTdhNzhhOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/dc84901d47b9c5438688ce8e8c7b6e1dee6aede2","sha":"dc84901d47b9c5438688ce8e8c7b6e1dee6aede2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/dc84901d47b9c5438688ce8e8c7b6e1dee6aede2"}],"sha":"5764190ecedfa0f2ef4686c528448e2f17a78a98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/5764190ecedfa0f2ef4686c528448e2f17a78a98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/dc84901d47b9c5438688ce8e8c7b6e1dee6aede2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:22:37Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:22:37Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"refactor: share AIS field widths, reuse derived charge, and correct the architecture notes\n\nThe AIS numeric field widths were declared twice, and one value appeared under\nthree names across the two AIS modules. They join the string widths already\nshared in aisUtils, and the AIS-local bounded-string copy folds into\nclampString, whose copy-forcing behavior it was the only thing adding.\n\nThe battery conversion derived the remaining charge for its time-remaining\nestimate, then omitted the remaining-capacity field it is. It now fills both, so\na pack publishing capacity.actual and stateOfCharge but not capacity.remaining\nreports its charge instead of \"not available\".\n\nCLAUDE.md had drifted in seven places, which matters because the file is treated\nas authoritative:\n\n- The module and PGN counts: 52 modules expanding to 83 runtime conversions\n  emitting 61 data PGNs, not 46, 76, and 53. There are no extra bus-layer PGNs;\n  pgnList announces only 126464.\n- The routeTypes entry described a module that no longer exists in that shape,\n  along with two route PGNs the plugin no longer emits.\n- The readiness section described a listener PluginManager does not own. index.ts\n  holds the single listener for the factory''s lifetime and forwards through\n  notifyNmea2000Ready, which is why no manager can leak one.\n- validation.ts documented a helper that does not exist and gave\n  resolveInstanceAndSource three parameters where it takes four.\n- The alert text and alert id constants were named and valued wrongly, and the\n  text cap''s stated reason was the encoder buffer rather than the fast-packet\n  limit that actually binds it.\n- AIS was described as the only delta-source module; the course conversions are\n  three more.\n\nAlso records the vessel-trip fuel behavior as deliberate. An unencodable fuel\ntotal drops the frame rather than publishing a range whose basis the frame\ncannot state, while an unencodable range still leaves a trustworthy fuel figure\nworth sending. The asymmetry was previously unexplained and read as an\noversight.","tree":{"sha":"ac2fe287abd287839b59d1c14a868fd8636a6144","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/ac2fe287abd287839b59d1c14a868fd8636a6144"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/dc84901d47b9c5438688ce8e8c7b6e1dee6aede2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/dc84901d47b9c5438688ce8e8c7b6e1dee6aede2","node_id":"C_kwDOQApVMtoAKGRjODQ5MDFkNDdiOWM1NDM4Njg4Y2U4ZThjN2I2ZTFkZWU2YWVkZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/cc6f97eb3f2c6146da6587987ca922e171b51295","sha":"cc6f97eb3f2c6146da6587987ca922e171b51295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/cc6f97eb3f2c6146da6587987ca922e171b51295"}],"sha":"dc84901d47b9c5438688ce8e8c7b6e1dee6aede2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/dc84901d47b9c5438688ce8e8c7b6e1dee6aede2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/cc6f97eb3f2c6146da6587987ca922e171b51295/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:08:37Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:08:37Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"refactor: remove duplicated logic, dead code, and stale reasoning\n\nThe own-vessel AIS reports asserted capabilities the plugin cannot know and no\nhardware backs: SOTDMA unit type, DSC capable, message 22 capable, and assigned\nAIS mode, the last of which claims a base station assigned the vessel a slot.\nSignal K describes no radio subtype or optional capability for the vessel, and\nthere is no physical transceiver behind these frames, so they now use the same\nconservative defaults ais.ts already documents for remote Class B targets.\n\nRemoved duplication and dead code:\n\n- windWeatherTrue carried a second hand-written copy of the PGN 130306 field\n  layout. It derives its angle from two inputs so it cannot use the conversion\n  factory, but the message shape now lives in one builder both call.\n- courseData hand-rolled the exact semantic of pathMatchesPrefix five times, and\n  rebuilt the self-context string on every server-wide delta as the first\n  statement of five conversions, for a value fixed for the process. ais.ts\n  already memoizes the same value and explains why.\n- The stop() loop clearing resendTimer off this.conversions could never fire:\n  wireConversion always builds a fresh spread, so the timer is set on the\n  per-start copy. this.timers is the authoritative teardown, which the comment\n  above it already said.\n- The Raymarine pending-clear cap was unreachable. That map is keyed by alarm\n  id, and alarmIdForPath can only return one of the ten ids in the fixed table,\n  so the table bounds it. The refresh to the newest end is kept and explained.\n- Tank levels used the shared instance normalizer, which takes a max precisely\n  so a caller can pass its own field width.\n\nCorrected reasoning that no longer matched the code. The alert text cap is set\nby the 223 byte fast-packet limit, not the encoder buffer: at 200 characters PGN\n126985 is already 221 payload bytes, so adding any omitted field would push it\nover. The PGN 127493 discrete status field is a plain 8-bit number in the pinned\nts-pgns, not a bit lookup. The pressure ceiling does not bound PGN 130314, whose\nfield is signed 32-bit at 0.1 Pa.\n\nAlso: conversion options now spread the user-controlled source and extras maps\nbefore the runtime flags, so a key literally named \"enabled\" or \"resend\" cannot\ndecide whether its own conversion runs. Days since the epoch floors rather than\ntruncates, since Math.trunc gives negative zero inside the last pre-epoch day\nand the guard that reads it does not catch that. The trim-tab normalizer moved\nto module scope instead of being rebuilt per delta, and two loops that only\nwanted an index stopped allocating a pair per iteration.","tree":{"sha":"ded9bd69662aa977ff1ed2513f89adfc574a52ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/ded9bd69662aa977ff1ed2513f89adfc574a52ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/cc6f97eb3f2c6146da6587987ca922e171b51295","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/cc6f97eb3f2c6146da6587987ca922e171b51295","node_id":"C_kwDOQApVMtoAKGNjNmY5N2ViM2YyYzYxNDZkYTY1ODc5ODdjYTkyMmUxNzFiNTEyOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/f67b3298797334f7327898cd7f1bcdc44977557a","sha":"f67b3298797334f7327898cd7f1bcdc44977557a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/f67b3298797334f7327898cd7f1bcdc44977557a"}],"sha":"cc6f97eb3f2c6146da6587987ca922e171b51295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/cc6f97eb3f2c6146da6587987ca922e171b51295"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/f67b3298797334f7327898cd7f1bcdc44977557a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:00:19Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T02:00:19Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix: correct alert eviction order, rudder order sign, and device id handling\n\nNotification alerts were evicted first-in rather than least-recently-seen.\nMap.set on an existing key keeps its original position, so an alert that kept\nrefreshing never moved, and at the 256 entry cap the victim was the longest\nrunning alert: an anchor alarm active for hours got a terminal clear on the\nchartplotter and then a fresh alert id on its next delta, so the alarm flapped.\nBoth the alert cache and the tracked-path map now delete before set, the same\nway ais.ts and raymarineAlarms.ts already keep their caps behaving as an LRU.\nThe regression test pins it: the anchor alarm keeps alert id 1 across a flood\nof 257 other alerts, where before it came back as 258.\n\nPGN 127245 angleOrder is a signed field carrying the same port and starboard\nconvention as position beside it, but the rudder conversion sent the magnitude\nand left the sign to the separate directionOrder enum. A receiver reading\nangleOrder on its own, which is the normal thing to do with a signed field, saw\na port order as starboard. Both angle fields are now range checked too.\n\nThree of the four electrical conversions rejected a numeric device id that solar\nand the engine conversions accept, so a Victron style electrical.chargers.0\ninstall silently produced no charger, inverter, or AC conversion at all. All\nfour now use the same permissive guard.\n\nAlso: transmission parameters tested the raw gear string rather than the mapped\none, so a gear with no GEAR_STATUS member and no oil readings emitted a frame\ncarrying only an instance, and attitude did the same when all three components\nwere invalid. The temperature conversions stamped the correlation SID that is\nmeant for related-PGN groups sampled at one instant, unlike every one of their\nenvironment siblings, so twelve unrelated sensors all claimed SID 87. Tank\nlevels reimplemented the shared instance normalizer instead of passing it the\n4-bit tank ceiling it already accepts, and dropped the canonical bait well group,\nwhich maps cleanly to Live well. Satellite azimuth is an unsigned field, so it\nnow normalizes rather than range checks, and a provider publishing signed\nazimuths keeps its western-hemisphere satellites.","tree":{"sha":"a59ddcb04f8cafec70795568fd8b895d6d660ab6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/a59ddcb04f8cafec70795568fd8b895d6d660ab6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/f67b3298797334f7327898cd7f1bcdc44977557a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/f67b3298797334f7327898cd7f1bcdc44977557a","node_id":"C_kwDOQApVMtoAKGY2N2IzMjk4Nzk3MzM0ZjczMjc4OThjZDdmMWJjZGM0NDk3NzU1N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/f9763bd9f0521d969847a0a709a5cf7948ca1cad","sha":"f9763bd9f0521d969847a0a709a5cf7948ca1cad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/f9763bd9f0521d969847a0a709a5cf7948ca1cad"}],"sha":"f67b3298797334f7327898cd7f1bcdc44977557a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/f67b3298797334f7327898cd7f1bcdc44977557a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/f9763bd9f0521d969847a0a709a5cf7948ca1cad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T01:49:22Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T01:49:22Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"fix: stop out-of-range and mistranslated values reaching the NMEA 2000 wire\n\nThe canboat encoder does not reject a finite value that will not fit a field,\nand it does not reject an unknown lookup label. It truncates the number modulo\nthe field width and encodes the unknown label as enum 0, so a bad input becomes\na plausible-looking wrong reading on the bus rather than a dropped frame.\nvalidateN2KMessage catches only NaN and Infinity, so nothing downstream caught\nthese.\n\nPGN 129029 carried both halves of the problem. Signal K and canboat spell the\nGNSS lookups differently, so Signal K''s own \"GNSS Fix\" encoded as enum 0, \"no\nGNSS\": a normal fix told every chartplotter on the bus there was no fix while a\nvalid position rode alongside it, and \"Combined GPS/GLONASS\" collapsed to plain\nGPS. Both lookups now translate through explicit tables and omit a value with no\ncanboat counterpart, which decodes as not available. Integrity is the exception:\nall four of its 2-bit codes are assigned, so an omitted field decodes as\n\"Unsafe\", and most installs never publish navigation.gnss.integrity at all. It\nnow falls back to the explicit no-checking code.\n\nThe unbounded numeric fields get the range check their guarded siblings already\nhad, with the wire ceiling named at each site:\n\n- SOG (PGN 129026) and drift (PGN 129291): -2 m/s decoded as 653.36 m/s.\n- Exhaust gas temperature (PGN 130312): 655.32 K is 382 C, which a dry-stack\n  probe exceeds under load, so 773 K went out as 117.64 K, a fabricated low\n  reading at the moment exhaust temperature matters most.\n- Temperature (PGNs 130310, 130312, and 130316) against each PGN''s own ceiling:\n  -5 K encoded as 650.36 K, hot enough to trip a receiver''s high-temp alarm.\n- Tank level (PGN 127505): a provider publishing percent instead of the Signal K\n  ratio scaled to 10000 and decoded as 38.528 percent.\n- Display brightness (PGN 126720): the same percent-versus-ratio mistake set a\n  real Raymarine backlight to 52 percent.\n- Depth offset (PGN 128267): the field reaches only about 32.7 m, so a larger\n  transducer offset wrapped and came out with the opposite sign.\n- Battery time remaining (PGN 127506): the 30 day clamp guarded only the derived\n  branch, so a Signal K supplied value reached the field unbounded.\n- Radio frequency and transmit power (PGN 129799), and the parsed IMO number\n  (PGN 129794), which is seven digits by definition.\n\nThree more fixes in the same area. Exhaust temperature had no freshness window,\nso a dead probe rebroadcast its last reading forever. The own-vessel AIS reports\nsent timestamp \"0\", a literal second-of-minute rather than the not-available\nsentinel its remote-target sibling uses. DSC distress calls resent every five\nseconds for as long as the provider left the path in place, so one inbound relay\nlooked like a continuing emergency; a distress call is an event, not a state.\n\nAlso aligns the humidity default identity table with the runtime it is supposed\nto describe. The table said instance 0 while both conversions emitted 100, so\nthe PGN 130313 collision check compared a pair the plugin never sends. Both now\nread one table, and the Raymarine brightness group id is validated with\nisValidSignalKId like its sibling electrical conversions, so an id containing a\ndot fails loudly instead of building a subscription path that never fires.","tree":{"sha":"78438c02e07f0dadbfd3608985ec1ca73cccad6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/78438c02e07f0dadbfd3608985ec1ca73cccad6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/f9763bd9f0521d969847a0a709a5cf7948ca1cad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/f9763bd9f0521d969847a0a709a5cf7948ca1cad","node_id":"C_kwDOQApVMtoAKGY5NzYzYmQ5ZjA1MjFkOTY5ODQ3YTBhNzA5YTVjZjc5NDhjYTFjYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/66a6d19698f7fae5ab6ec89d6cb1ef9709bdf4f0","sha":"66a6d19698f7fae5ab6ec89d6cb1ef9709bdf4f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/66a6d19698f7fae5ab6ec89d6cb1ef9709bdf4f0"}],"sha":"f9763bd9f0521d969847a0a709a5cf7948ca1cad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/f9763bd9f0521d969847a0a709a5cf7948ca1cad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/66a6d19698f7fae5ab6ec89d6cb1ef9709bdf4f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T01:25:59Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T01:25:59Z","email":"NearlCrews@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Nearl Crews"},"message":"refactor(panel): move the setup wizard and feedback surfaces onto shared primitives\n\nThe setup wizard was a hand-built modal carrying its own scrim, focus trap,\nEscape handler, and focus return. It is now a shared Dialog, which owns all of\nthat plus visual-viewport sizing, the narrow-panel bottom-sheet layout, scroll\ncontainment, and nested overlay layering. The browser check opens it and proves\nthe contract: it portals inside the owning panel root, moves focus into itself,\npasses axe with its proposal list rendered, and returns focus to its trigger.\n\nThe rest of the pass replaces panel copies of shared behavior. Error notices in\nthe advisor, the wizard, and the conversion detail become Banner, which adds a\nvisible severity symbol and screen-reader severity text. The advisor Review now\nbutton, its QuestDB connection test, and the path inventory refresh become\nButton with loading state, so the accessible name stays stable while the\noperation runs instead of the label changing mid-interaction. Advisor toggles\nbecome Checkbox with their help text as a wired description, and the advisor and\nglobal number fields become LabeledField, replacing a visible span paired with a\nduplicate aria-label that had already drifted out of sync. The panel root now\ntakes its font family from the shared token rather than a local stack.\n\nThe dense conversion rows keep their local controls: the shared controls carry a\n40 pixel minimum height, so adopting them there would be a visual redesign of the\n34 pixel row rather than an adoption.\n\nTwo follow-on changes fall out of the Dialog. The panel chunk budget moves from\n48 kB to 65 kB brotli, because the React Aria overlay stack the Dialog needs adds\nabout 15 kB to a bundle the local Signal K server hands to the admin UI over the\nLAN. The bundle smoke test now stubs the small set of DOM members React Aria\ntouches during its module-level setup, since that context declares window and\ndocument without a DOM behind them.\n\nAlso fixes a missing space in the footer validation notice, drops the now-unused\nmodal backdrop and shadow tokens, and hoists the duplicated shared UI version\nassertion out of both panel check scripts.","tree":{"sha":"0a2b7dfa6a99bab9c3d75a6b7cdebc2868eab1ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/0a2b7dfa6a99bab9c3d75a6b7cdebc2868eab1ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/66a6d19698f7fae5ab6ec89d6cb1ef9709bdf4f0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews","id":23341701,"login":"NearlCrews","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMzQxNzAx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/66a6d19698f7fae5ab6ec89d6cb1ef9709bdf4f0","node_id":"C_kwDOQApVMtoAKDY2YTZkMTk2OThmN2ZhZTVhYjZlYzg5ZDZjYjFlZjk3MDliZGY0ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commit/51a3c91854f5179c9696ced7e759194d5a2e08f1","sha":"51a3c91854f5179c9696ced7e759194d5a2e08f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/51a3c91854f5179c9696ced7e759194d5a2e08f1"}],"sha":"66a6d19698f7fae5ab6ec89d6cb1ef9709bdf4f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/commits/66a6d19698f7fae5ab6ec89d6cb1ef9709bdf4f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/even