-lane code review:\n\n1. notifications.ts: stale alertId leak when upstream changes alertId for\n   the same path. The old alertId was never released from pgnsByAlertId,\n   emitTracker, usedAlertIds, or alertIdToPath, causing ghost PGNs that\n   could never be cleared and reverse-map corruption that could delete\n   the wrong path binding on eviction. Fix: releaseAlertId(oldAlertId)\n   before registering the new id.\n\n2. bearingDistanceBetweenMarks.ts: the true-bearing path passed the raw\n   value to the unsigned uint16 bearingOriginToDestination field without\n   toUnsignedAngle normalization. A negative or >2pi bearing would encode\n   as a wrong direction on the wire. The magnetic-bearing fallback path\n   already called normalizeAngle; the sibling PGN 129284 in\n   navigationData.ts already used toUnsignedAngle. Fix: wrap with\n   toUnsignedAngle. Added regression test for -0.5 rad -> 5.7832 rad.\n\n3. ais.ts generateStatic: the length, beam, fromBow, and draft fields\n   were passed raw to the PGN encoder. A NaN or Infinity from a flaky\n   provider would fail validateN2KMessage and drop the entire PGN 129794\n   instead of emitting the field as ''not available''. The sibling\n   aisExtended.ts already wrapped these fields with toFiniteOrUndefined.\n   Fix: wrap all four fields with toFiniteOrUndefined.","tree":{"sha":"6ebb7621612b1e037de0e9a0eaff2d9e992ca562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/trees/6ebb7621612b1e037de0e9a0eaff2d9e992ca562"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NearlCrews/signalk-nmea2000-emitter-cannon/git/commits/bf108e8fba5a325e538f7a492e2fdb8ca6cd5fd1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23341701?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NearlCrews/followers","following_url":