tions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgheithcock","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dharunashokkumar/K25KM-Connect/commits/a41db04d2746ab549d056db4ede4cd803f64989c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-09-29T21:29:32Z","email":"jgheithcock@gmail.com","name":"JG Heithcock"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-09-29T21:29:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MM 65084 server-side (#33861)\n\n* MM-65084: (server-side) PKCE code-exchange for SSO\n\nServer side changes needed for MM-65084. Guarded by MobileSSOCodeExchange feature flag.\n\n* Update users.yaml for vet-api testing\n\n* Change error for not saving SAML token to existing generic ''can''t save token'' message\n\n* Restricting to sha256 only PKCEs\n\n* Change out PKCE terminology to SAML\n\nThis came out as Claude used \"PKCE\" as a shorthand for the style and I did not know better. SAML is the correct term here.\nThis also fixes a linter issue where we were assigning `codeVerifier` to `computed` but then overwriting it in all cases (so that was misleading and unecessary)\n\n* Adding ConsumeTokenOnce and IsExpired as suggested by security review\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a5437947ff1cfd8d6d10e9acd711c421be57347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dharunashokkumar/K25KM-Connect/git/trees/7a5437947ff1cfd8d6d10e9acd711c421be57347"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dharunashokkumar/K25KM-Connect/git/commits/a41db04d2746ab549d056db4ede4cd803f64989c","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a5437947ff1cfd8d6d10e9acd711c421be57347\nparent a95be3d76e9035715eef5ef0e5f93c8fdf63f8c5\nauthor JG Heithcock <jgheithcock@gmail.com> 1759181372 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1759181372 -0700\n\nMM 65084 server-side (#33861)\n\n* MM-65084: (server-side) PKCE code-exchange for SSO\n\nServer side changes needed for MM-65084. Guarded by MobileSSOCodeExchange feature flag.\n\n* Update users.yaml for vet-api testing\n\n* Change error for not saving SAML token to existing generic ''can''t save token'' message\n\n* Restricting to sha256 only PKCEs\n\n* Change out PKCE terminology to SAML\n\nThis came out as Claude used \"PKCE\" as a shorthand for the style and I did not know better. SAML is the correct term here.\nThis also fixes a linter issue where we were assigning `codeVerifier` to `computed` but then overwriting it in all cases (so that was misleading and unecessary)\n\n* Adding ConsumeTokenOnce and IsExpired as suggested by security review\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJo2vo9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhlwQABTSWjwAKGewhv0MEM2xeU53\nB/ae6vg0ji0MaIgbUzouFBgn7BHqZYWd9vLMzNRYXSyE26tHBVlhn+tjtsdRF3dt\n+hOobhBzzeyDNXIXS9EI4I8glgnAAmlmuZ7FCasD+NgHi5J7JtDA4w0b5cMfaEwo\n8Su3eyg1nwCXs0fPtq7I6pcTVPL8K9iYJhuOvqznGJxBW1Jk+wuq1MJFeJ+JEPgO\nVOQLcD272uaG/pZkiOcaqsgW4ho4glg9261wq3p8xb/Ad4gayIUG5qQGOrD1Ry4n\nMvIlcWy0BdIey2eQtGMzJsnuLNYArq56YBDrt+IAZzoRNR3OBGm6ZI9PQwyt+YSU\n4PX60GUseMwUDj0AVPo5rzZvV+23yBEOQVcDslDnWnDZliQ+iezbhVKGMGwRQ5lP\nGMmUGqkpj4Qff8/jawF5zYbRulYmw7Q9vrKCZt1fVUagWyRRu9UYJsC0IBF4isQf\nmi845K7XYlFh65bDFbT3m4W5M9MSV2qvePKFap+boi5/3ziQLz/llqfTlWecWtk1\nP+JN/igUFxXFG1FgAKPdvdM/yLCzjsABr7J/sM2YodNkTVcVx4iZZf9ADqDoGcXg\nTtGSkgco43hBndFVqdwPoLaIA4VERDKI2KTBZatcCCcZ11RyOAJNOEg0j4baz1YJ\n8Hf7RHHUBaRm1Ee2Ejnq\n=I+fy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-10-12T11:52:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"l